    "Three samples per profile/surface expose ordinary network and browser variability; medians are observations, not a latency guarantee or a statistical significance claim.",
    "The comparison is Chromium desktop and emulated Pixel 7 on the same macOS host, not a physical mobile-device qualification.",
    "First useful content is the documented DOM/paint-opportunity metric; header interactivity is separate. This is not Lighthouse LCP or a complete Core Web Vitals study.",
    "Decoded script response bytes include reused browser-cache bodies and do not measure parsing, decoding or Worker CPU time.",
    "Anonymous public and stored status-read behavior only: no authenticated/private app, document/provider journey, billed-cost or forced collector qualification.",
    "Some initial-homepage and status timing ranges overlap before/after. Three samples do not justify generalizing their latency changes; the robust measured result is the removal of document/script requests during public page changes, whose timing ranges are entirely separated in these samples."
